ProsperoSunshine: send controller feedback without waiting for the next control event

The control loop only looks at the feedback queue between events, and with a 150 ms timeout that means
every ping, about 100 ms apart. moonlight-common-c keeps only the newest of the rumble messages it finds
queued, so a shorter pulse arrived as its stop alone and the client never rumbled.

--- a/src/stream.cpp
+++ b/src/stream.cpp
@@ -1392,7 +1392,11 @@
         break;
       }
 
+#ifdef __SCE__
+      server->iterate(5ms);
+#else
       server->iterate(150ms);
+#endif
     }
 
     // Let all remaining connections know the server is shutting down
